        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4460,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1986,
        "paragraph_id": "22DE40E7",
        "text": "Since in both hydrostatic and non-hydrostatic groundwater flow some local velocities may exceed the critical Reynolds number for the start of turbulence (Recrit), the turbulent hydraulic conductivity (K) is updated using the local Reynolds number. The solution to (C.15) and the update of the turbulent hydraulic conductivity are iterated until a minimum threshold difference between iterations is found. Note that this approach is only used is the turbulent groundwater model is selected (keyword: gwscheme = turbulent)."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 92559,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4462,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1988,
        "paragraph_id": "386E71B7",
        "text": "The (iterated) solution for the specific vertical discharge is used to update the groundwater level and surface water level:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 92659,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4466,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1992,
        "paragraph_id": "33A068D8",
        "text": "If the groundwater and surface water are connected, and the submarine exchange from the surface water to the groundwater estimated in (C.27) is greater than the amount of surface water available in the cell, continuity is enforced by lowering the groundwater level to compensate for the lack of permeating water:"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
